  <h2>First paint: SPA spinner instead of static reassurance</h2>
  <p>
    The payload mounts a <code>#app</code> root whose children are only a <strong>centred loading spinner</strong> (<code>.half-circle-spinner</code>) until deferred bundles execute.
    Deferred chunks explicitly reference <strong>Vue</strong>, <strong>iView</strong>, vendor code, and an application bundle—classic single-page architecture where perceived speed hinges on JS download + hydration latency rather than immediate HTML prose.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>UX takeaway:</strong> impatient Spreadsheet buyers mentally rehearsing &ldquo;paste URL → instant preview&rdquo; should expect an interim spinner whenever caches miss or connectivity degrades; it is not an outage signal by itself.
    Carry the same patience mantra from our <a href="/blog/kakobuy-links-discovery-url-hygiene/">URL hygiene primer</a>: marketplace identity matters more than how quickly chrome renders chrome.
  </p>

  <h2>Bot friction vs signup delight</h2>
  <p>
